B.b81=new A.hH("Data on your device",'Player names, rounds, scores, records and settings are stored only on your device and are not transmitted. You can remove them at any time via "Delete history" or by uninstalling the app. There is no user account.')
B.b83=new A.hH("Online leaderboard",'Only if you explicitly choose "Submit" after a round, the following data is transmitted: the display name you choose, the strokes per hole and in total, the venue and the time. The entry is visible to all users of the app. No device ID and no account is stored.\n\nThe data is stored by the service provider Supabase on servers in the EU. For technical reasons the server briefly processes your IP address. The legal basis is your consent (Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR), which you can withdraw at any time. Only the 50 best rounds per month and venue are kept; previous months remain visible as an archive. For the daily ranking, the 20 best rounds of the current day are kept as well; they are deleted automatically afterwards unless they are in the monthly ranking. The daily ranking shows only the display name and strokes, no time. We will delete your entry on request \u2013 just send us an email.')
B.b7U=new A.hH("Push notifications","In the Android and iOS app we use Firebase Cloud Messaging by Google to send notifications from the venue. This processes a random device identifier (token) together with the selected language. Google may also process data in the USA; the transfer is based on the EU-US Data Privacy Framework. You can turn off notifications in your device settings at any time.")
B.b7S=new A.hH("Video in the rules","The explanatory video is provided by YouTube (Google). Data such as your IP address is only transmitted to YouTube when you play it.")
B.b7W=new A.hH("Links to other apps","Call, email, directions, website and Facebook open other apps or websites. Their privacy policies apply there.")
B.b7Z=new A.hH("Your rights","You have the right to access, rectification, erasure, restriction of processing, data portability and objection, and to withdraw your consent. Please contact the email address above. You can also lodge a complaint with the Austrian Data Protection Authority (www.dsb.gv.at).")
